const decks=[
{id:'odd-eyes',name:'Odd-Eyes',subtitle:'Pendulum scales · Xyz · Link',boss:'Odd-Eyes Override Dragon',art:'https://images.ygoprodeck.com/images/cards_cropped/58083496.jpg',product:'Legendary ARC-V Decks',fixed:'40-card Main Deck + 15-card Extra Deck',playstyle:'Pendulum combo · Xyz · Link · Fusion',bonus:'One random duplicate from six Odd-Eyes bonus candidates; Secret Rare, with a chance at Starlight Rare.',official:'https://www.db.yugioh-card.com/yugiohdb/card_search.action?ope=1&pid=2000001679000&request_locale=en&rp=99999',keys:['Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragon','Odd-Eyes Persona Dragon','Odd-Eyes Mirage Dragon','Odd-Eyes Revolution Dragon','Performapal Odd-Eyes Seer','Sky Iris','Odd-Eyes Absolute Dragon','Odd-Eyes Override Dragon'],listNote:'The official Included In page is set-wide, so it verifies card identities but does not sort each print into a deck or give copy counts. Konami’s strategy guide confirms this is a ready-to-play 40 + 15 deck and describes its Pendulum/Link plan. Use the physical sealed list for exact quantities.',combos:[
{title:'Two scales into Odd-Eyes Absolute Dragon',hand:'Odd-Eyes Persona Dragon + Odd-Eyes Mirage Dragon (or another included high scale) + 2 Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragons',condition:'No cards are needed on your field; the two Level 7 monsters must be in your hand.',steps:['Activate Persona Dragon as the low scale and Mirage Dragon as the high scale. The scale range includes Level 7.','Pendulum Summon both Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragons from your hand.','Overlay the two Level 7 monsters to Xyz Summon Odd-Eyes Absolute Dragon. Keep its material attached for its attack-negation effect.'],result:'Odd-Eyes Absolute Dragon, with 2 Xyz Materials attached.'},
{title:'Build with an extra Pendulum Summon',hand:'Any card to discard for Odd-Eyes Override Dragon; on the field, 2+ monsters (including a Pendulum Monster) for its Link Summon plus another Pendulum Monster Card to destroy',condition:'Have two or more monsters available, including a Pendulum Monster, for the Link Summon. This is a mid-combo route, not a one-card opener.',steps:['Link Summon Odd-Eyes Override Dragon using at least 2 monsters, including a Pendulum Monster.','Activate Override Dragon to destroy another card you control and draw 1 card. If the destroyed card was a Pendulum Monster Card, gain an additional Pendulum Summon for Performapal, Magician Pendulum, and Odd-Eyes monsters.','Conduct the additional Pendulum Summon for eligible monsters from your hand or face-up Extra Deck.','During your turn, when your opponent activates a card or effect, discard a card to activate Override Dragon’s Quick Effect and negate that activation.'],result:'Odd-Eyes Override Dragon plus a conditional extra Pendulum Summon and a turn-time negate.'},
{title:'Make Odd-Eyes Vortex Dragon',hand:'A Pendulum Scale pair (one 6 or lower, one 9 or higher) + Performapal Odd-Eyes Dissolver + Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragon',condition:'The scales must include Levels 7 and 8. Dissolver is Level 8; Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragon is Level 7; Odd-Eyes Vortex Dragon is in the Extra Deck.',steps:['Activate two Pendulum Scales that bracket Levels 7 and 8, such as Scale 1 and Scale 12.','Pendulum Summon Performapal Odd-Eyes Dissolver and Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragon from your hand.','Activate Dissolver’s monster effect. Fusion Summon Odd-Eyes Vortex Dragon using Dissolver as the Pendulum Monster material and Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragon as the Odd-Eyes material.'],result:'Odd-Eyes Vortex Dragon Fusion Summoned using Performapal Odd-Eyes Dissolver and Odd-Eyes Arc Pendulum Dragon.'}]},
{id:'lunalight',name:'Lunalight',subtitle:'Fusion · recovery · pressure',boss:'Lunalight Liger Dancer',art:'https://images.ygoprodeck.com/images/cards_cropped/54701958.jpg',product:'Legendary ARC-V Decks',fixed:'40-card Main Deck + 15-card Extra Deck',playstyle:'Fusion combo · GY recovery · board pressure',bonus:'One random duplicate from six Lunalight bonus candidates; Secret Rare, with a chance at Starlight Rare.',official:'https://www.db.yugioh-card.com/yugiohdb/card_search.action?ope=1&pid=2000001679000&request_locale=en&rp=99999',keys:['Lunalight Gold Leo','Lunalight Yellow Marten','Lunalight Masquerade','Lunalight Silver Hound','Lunalight Kaleido Chick','Lunalight Tiger','Lunalight Black Sheep','Polymerization','Lunalight Liger Dancer'],listNote:'The official Included In page verifies the Lunalight card pool, while Konami’s product guide confirms the single-deck 40 + 15 structure and identifies the featured combo cards. Its published Gold Leo route below is described by Konami as a one-card combo. Consult the physical product list for exact card quantities.',combos:[
{title:'Gold Leo: one-card route to two Liger Dancers',hand:'Lunalight Gold Leo',condition:'The route uses its Normal Summon and specified cards in the Deck/Extra Deck; it assumes the effects resolve and the listed targets remain available.',steps:['Normal Summon Gold Leo. Add Yellow Marten from the Deck, then discard it; Yellow Marten adds Lunalight Masquerade.','Masquerade sends Silver Hound, whose effect Special Summons Kaleido Chick. Chick sends Tiger from the Deck; Gold Leo returns Tiger to your hand. Yellow Marten Special Summons itself by returning Chick to your hand.','Xyz Summon Tiger King with Yellow Marten and Gold Leo. Set Tenki, then add Black Sheep.','Discard Black Sheep to add Polymerization. Place Tiger in a Pendulum Zone and activate its effect to Special Summon Black Sheep from the GY.','Fuse the Kaleido Chick in your hand and Black Sheep on your field into Perfume Dancer. Resolve the Fusion Material effects to recover Chick and Polymerization; Perfume Dancer adds Luna Light Perfume and can revive Chick after returning Tiger to your hand.','Continue through Cross-Sheep and Wolf’s Pendulum Fusion Effect to make two Liger Dancers and the listed follow-up board.'],result:'Two Lunalight Liger Dancers, with follow-up options. See the official linked guide for the complete line and exact trigger order.'},
{title:'Going second: Lunalight Fusion into Liger Dancer',hand:'Lunalight Fusion + 2 Lunalight monsters',condition:'Opponent controls a monster Special Summoned from the Extra Deck; the Extra Deck contains Lunalight Leo Dancer and Liger Dancer.',steps:['Activate Lunalight Fusion and select two Lunalight monsters from your hand/field, Lunalight Leo Dancer from your Extra Deck, and one Lunalight monster from your Deck as materials.','Resolve the Fusion Summon of Lunalight Liger Dancer; its materials are Leo Dancer plus 3 Lunalight monsters.','If the opponent still controls Special Summoned monsters, Liger Dancer can send a Lunalight monster from your Extra Deck to the GY to destroy those monsters.'],result:'Lunalight Liger Dancer; the line uses the opponent’s Extra Deck monster as the condition that unlocks a Deck/Extra Deck material.'},
{title:'Scarlet Tiger turns a Lunalight effect into Polymerization',hand:'Lunalight Scarlet Tiger + a Lunalight monster effect + two other Lunalight monsters',condition:'For Tiger to add Polymerization, your opponent must have activated a card or effect during the same turn. The monsters and Fusion Spell must remain available.',steps:['Activate a Lunalight monster effect, such as Gold Leo’s search/discard effect.','Chain/activate Scarlet Tiger’s hand effect to Special Summon it; if the opponent activated a card/effect this turn, add Polymerization from Deck or GY.','Use Polymerization with two available Lunalight monsters (and Tiger if useful) to Fusion Summon a Lunalight Fusion Monster whose material requirement is met.'],result:'A live Polymerization access route that can recover when the opponent interacts.'}]},
{id:'speedroid',name:'Speedroid',subtitle:'WIND Tuners · Synchro · Pendulum',boss:'Crystal Clear Wing Over Synchro Dragon',art:'https://images.ygoprodeck.com/images/cards_cropped/84343351.jpg',product:'Legendary ARC-V Decks',fixed:'40-card Main Deck + 15-card Extra Deck',playstyle:'WIND Synchro combo · Tuners · interaction',bonus:'One random duplicate from six Speedroid bonus candidates; Secret Rare, with a chance at Starlight Rare.',official:'https://www.db.yugioh-card.com/yugiohdb/card_search.action?ope=1&pid=2000001679000&request_locale=en&rp=99999',keys:['Speedroid Terrortop','Speedroid Marble Machine','Speedroid Taketomborg','Speedroid Red-Eyed Dice','Speedroid Wing Synchron','Speedroid Darumaknocker','Clear Wing Synchro Dragon','Crystal Clear Wing Over Synchro Dragon'],listNote:'The official Included In page verifies the Speedroid card pool. Konami’s strategy guide confirms 3 Terrortop, 3 Marble Machine, 3 Speedroid Scratch, 2 Darumaknocker, and 2 Hi-Speedroid Rubber Band Shooter; it also explains the following lines.',combos:[
{title:'Terrortop alone into a Level 7 Clear Wing',hand:'Speedroid Terrortop',condition:'You control no monsters and have your Normal Summon available. Taketomborg, Red-Eyed Dice, and Clear Wing Synchro Dragon remain in Deck/Extra Deck.',steps:['Special Summon Terrortop because you control no monsters; add Speedroid Marble Machine from Deck.','Normal Summon Marble Machine and add Speedroid Taketomborg. Special Summon Taketomborg because you control a WIND monster.','Tribute Taketomborg to Special Summon Speedroid Red-Eyed Dice from Deck.','Use Dice’s effect to target Terrortop and change its Level to 6.','Synchro Summon Clear Wing Synchro Dragon using Level 1 Dice + Level 6 Terrortop. Taketomborg restricts further Special Summons to WIND monsters this turn; Clear Wing is WIND.'],result:'Clear Wing Synchro Dragon, a Level 7 monster with disruption against certain Level 5+ monster effects.'},
{title:'Two Pendulum Scales directly make Clear Wing',hand:'Speedroid Wing Synchron + Speedroid Marble Machine',condition:'Both cards are in hand and the Clear Wing Synchro Dragon is in your Extra Deck.',steps:['Activate Speedroid Wing Synchron and Speedroid Marble Machine in your Pendulum Zones. Marble Machine is a Level 2 WIND Pendulum Monster.','Activate Wing Synchron’s Pendulum Effect: destroy both cards, then Special Summon Clear Wing Synchro Dragon from the Extra Deck. This is treated as a Synchro Summon.'],result:'Clear Wing Synchro Dragon without first summoning monsters to the field.'},
{title:'Marble Machine plus Taketomborg into a Synchro',hand:'Speedroid Marble Machine + Speedroid Taketomborg',condition:'You have not used your Normal Summon; Red-Eyed Dice and a Level 5 Synchro Monster remain available.',steps:['Normal Summon Marble Machine and add Speedroid Red-Eyed Dice from Deck.','Special Summon Taketomborg because Marble Machine is a WIND monster. Tribute Taketomborg to Special Summon Red-Eyed Dice from Deck.','Dice changes Marble Machine’s Level from 2 to 4. Tune Level 1 Dice with Level 4 Marble Machine for the Level 5 Hi-Speedroid Chanbara.'],result:'Hi-Speedroid Chanbara; the WIND-only lock from Taketomborg is compatible with the Synchro Monster.'}]},
{id:'chronicles',name:'Fallen & the Virtuous',subtitle:'Branded Fusion · Fallen of Albaz',boss:'Mirrorjade the Iceblade Dragon',art:'https://images.ygoprodeck.com/images/cards_cropped/44146295.jpg',product:'THE CHRONICLES DECK: The Fallen & The Virtuous (All-Foil Edition)',fixed:'40-card Main Deck + 10-card Extra Deck',playstyle:'Branded Fusion combo · midrange · interaction',bonus:'One random second copy of one of six fixed Ultra Rares; Secret Rare, with a chance at Starlight Rare. The extra copy is optional.',official:'https://www.db.yugioh-card.com/yugiohdb/card_search.action?ope=1&pid=2000001544000&request_locale=en&rp=99999',keys:['Branded Fusion','Fallen of Albaz','Despian Tragedy','Lubellion the Searing Dragon','Mirrorjade the Iceblade Dragon','Albion the Branded Dragon','Branded in White','The Fallen & The Virtuous'],listNote:'The official product page confirms 50 fixed cards and a random duplicate; the official included-card list shows all fixed identities. For a legal TCG build, sort Fusion/Synchro/Xyz/Link monsters into the Extra Deck, keep 40–60 cards in the Main Deck, check copy limits, and register a legal configuration. The sealed product is a card pool; it is not a 50-card Main Deck.',combos:[
{title:'Branded Fusion into Mirrorjade',hand:'Branded Fusion + any card to discard for Lubellion',condition:'Branded Fusion is in hand; Fallen of Albaz and Despian Tragedy are in the Deck; Lubellion and Mirrorjade are in the Extra Deck.',steps:['Activate Branded Fusion. Send Fallen of Albaz and Despian Tragedy from Deck to GY to Fusion Summon Lubellion the Searing Dragon.','After the Chain resolves, Despian Tragedy’s trigger can add a Despia monster from Deck to hand because it was sent to the GY by a card effect.','Activate Lubellion’s Fusion effect by discarding 1 card. Shuffle Lubellion and Fallen of Albaz as Fusion Materials to Fusion Summon Mirrorjade. Fallen of Albaz returns to the Main Deck; Lubellion returns to the Extra Deck.','Branded Fusion restricts Extra Deck Special Summons to Fusion Monsters for the rest of the turn; this line stays within that restriction.'],result:'Mirrorjade the Iceblade Dragon plus a Despia search, if Tragedy’s effect resolves.'},
{title:'Fallen of Albaz uses an opponent’s LIGHT monster',hand:'Fallen of Albaz + 1 discard card',condition:'Opponent controls a face-up LIGHT monster usable as Fusion Material; Albion the Branded Dragon and Mirrorjade the Iceblade Dragon are in your Extra Deck.',steps:['Normal or Special Summon Fallen of Albaz.','Activate its on-summon effect and discard 1 card as the activation cost.','Fusion Summon Albion the Branded Dragon using Fallen of Albaz and the opponent’s LIGHT monster.','Use Albion’s Fusion effect to banish Albion from your field and Fallen of Albaz from your GY; Fusion Summon Mirrorjade the Iceblade Dragon.'],result:'Mirrorjade the Iceblade Dragon; Albion and Fallen of Albaz are banished as its Fusion Materials, and the opponent’s LIGHT monster remains in the GY.'},
{title:'Nadir Servant sets an Albaz follow-up',hand:'Nadir Servant',condition:'Titaniklad the Ash Dragon is in your Extra Deck and a Dogmatika monster or Fallen of Albaz is in your Deck/GY with ATK no greater than Titaniklad.',steps:['Activate Nadir Servant: send Titaniklad from Extra Deck to the GY, then add a legal Dogmatika monster or Fallen of Albaz from Deck/GY.','For the rest of the turn after it resolves, you cannot Special Summon from the Extra Deck. Do not attempt a Fusion line this turn.','During the End Phase, Titaniklad’s effect can add or Special Summon a Dogmatika monster or Fallen of Albaz from your Deck.'],result:'A next-turn Albaz starter or Dogmatika follow-up; this is a setup line, not an immediate Extra Deck combo.'}]}
];
